ow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come on guys.. Try to be serious here.. please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you're talking about high-caliber weapons in the hands of elves and dwarves.<br /> <br /> How can we not take that seriously? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:28:59-07:00","id":936338,"title":"","content":"Since elves especailly seem smart enough, it shouldn't be THAT hard to train some of their best/brightest..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T20:00:32-07:00","id":936382,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine any Tolkien elves signing up to be taught by humans. But even if they did, only loadout 6 offers more than a handful of guns to train them with, and every bullet spent training is one less to use in battle.<br /> <br /> And the battles are already won, without guns. It seems like the only reason to have the choice would be if you wanted to slaughter the other side and change the fate of Middle-Earth. Otherwise you're just taking a momentous event in your life, being transported into a fictional world, and the one thing you choose to do is kill a bunch of people and monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T22:52:07-07:00","id":936430,"title":"","content":"When i first came up with this brain teaser, it WAS cause of a dream of potentially changing the fate of a major battle (or two)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:30:38-07:00","id":941211,"title":"","content":"One (1) mobile ICBM launch vehicle with a wide-targeting MIRV warhead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T18:22:27-07:00","id":941568,"title":"","content":"Arming hobbits with grenades would change Middle Earth in a hurry. They<i> are</i> known for their skill as stone throwers, after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:21:35-07:00","id":941609,"title":"","content":"Considering the numbers of the battle and the amount of ammo you're listing, I don't think it's enough to turn the battle of Minas Tirith or Helm's Deep. Minas Tirith had an army of 30,000 and at Helm's Deep it was 10,000. I really don't think it would change the battle that much, personally.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:49:24-07:00","id":942128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/934687-which-weapon-s-load-out-would-you-take-for-a-battle-at-helm-s-deep-or-minas-tirith?p=941609#post941609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the numbers of the battle and the amount of ammo you're listing, I don't think it's enough to turn the battle of Minas Tirith or Helm's Deep. Minas Tirith had an army of 30,000 and at Helm's Deep it was 10,000. I really don't think it would change the battle that much, personally.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, the # of rounds overall are not in the 1 bullet per enemy camp, but can you imagine the scene as some Orai see three of their comrades killed by one 50 cal shot ripping through them? Or 20 or more flying around after a 40mm grenade goes boom!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:15:41-07:00","id":942145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/934687-which-weapon-s-load-out-would-you-take-for-a-battle-at-helm-s-deep-or-minas-tirith?p=942128#post942128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, the # of rounds overall are not in the 1 bullet per enemy camp, but can you imagine the scene as some Orai see three of their comrades killed by one 50 cal shot ripping through them? Or 20 or more flying around after a 40mm grenade goes boom!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find gun and explosive warfare all that exciting, to be honest. I prefer the sword and sorcery large scale battles, personally. Seeing a large stone hurled by a catapult and rolling over a couple dozen orks is much more satisfying to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T02:49:27-07:00","id":942592,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This is based off a few assumptions:<br /> 1: That we know how the battles will turn out<br /> 2: We deliberately want to change the outcome<br /> 3: The equipment has soldiers that come with them or there are already personnel in Middle Earth proficient with these weapons (\u2018cuz reasons)<br /> <br /> I\u2019m choosing Loadout Three. In both of the aforementioned battles, things went bad as soon as the gates were breached. During the Battle of Helms Deep, the goal will be to use snipers to take down the grenade-runners (beserkers?) and prevent them from reaching the wall. During the Battle of Minas Tirith (sp?) the objectives will be similar, but the claymores will be set around/in front of the gate. The goal here will be take down the battering ram before it can be used. Also, if I have the option, all snipers will be female.<br /> <br /> Did you ever read <i>Grunts</i>?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:59:08-07:00","id":942640,"title":"","content":"3 doesn't seem like a given.<br /> <br /> Yes. There was a magic curse involved there, however. That's how everyone learned how to use the weapons and become so orderly so fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:14:56-07:00","id":942746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> : Yeah, I pulled that assumption from a chimerical nihil. It was either that or assume I'm Frank Castle. Without anyone who knows how to use them, none of these weapons do much good. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:55:05-07:00","id":943240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/934687-which-weapon-s-load-out-would-you-take-for-a-battle-at-helm-s-deep-or-minas-tirith?p=942592#post942592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This is based off a few assumptions:<br /> 1: That we know how the battles will turn out<br /> 2: We deliberately want to change the outcome<br /> 3: The equipment has soldiers that come with them or there are already personnel in Middle Earth proficient with these weapons (\u2018cuz reasons)<br /> <br /> I\u2019m choosing Loadout Three. In both of the aforementioned battles, things went bad as soon as the gates were breached. During the Battle of Helms Deep, the goal will be to use snipers to take down the grenade-runners (beserkers?) and prevent them from reaching the wall. During the Battle of Minas Tirith (sp?) the objectives will be similar, but the claymores will be set around/in front of the gate. The goal here will be take down the battering ram before it can be used. Also, if I have the option, all snipers will be female.<br /> <br /> Did you ever read <i>Grunts</i>?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes we know what we know now.. So if you have not seen the films OR read the novels, you are going in just as blind as the locals are!!!<br /> 2) that is a good assumption.<br /> 3) a good teacher can easily school a smart student in 3-5 hrs for some of those weapons. BUT lets say you had a full day.<br /> Do you think teaching a bunch of elves would really be that hard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:14:45-07:00","id":943436,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">My concern with training isn't the ability of the students but the resources of the instructor; I'd need to use the bullets I brought with me to train those elves. Elves are smart, but I'm guessing that centuries of personal training with elven bows isn't going to lend well to firearms-adaptability. In the original Battle of Helms Deep, all it took was one beserker to breach the gate, so I'd want every round I could get. <br /> Now, if I had a day AND ammunition specifically for training, then I'd say <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">eezy peezy.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:49:32-07:00","id":944059,"title":"","content":"I don't need to see anyone or dodge, I'll rock a C4 vest like my ancestors did and blow everyone up.<br /> <br /> (this is just a joke by the way, cant say anything without offending people nowadays lmao)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T07:23:17-07:00","id":944297,"title":"","content":"I was in a thread at /k/ where /tg/ asked them this very question.<br /> The result was basically Trench Warfare meets Siege Warfare, with Orcs getting slaughtered by machine gun fire and artillery.<br /> An Irony I'm sure J.R.R. himself would appreciate (or despise), being a WWI Vet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:46:44-07:00","id":944435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/934687-which-weapon-s-load-out-would-you-take-for-a-battle-at-helm-s-deep-or-minas-tirith?p=944297#post944297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was in a thread at /k/ where /tg/ asked them this very question.<br /> The result was basically Trench Warfare meets Siege Warfare, with Orcs getting slaughtered by machine gun fire and artillery.<br /> An Irony I'm sure J.R.R. himself would appreciate (or despise), being a WWI Vet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure whether he would like that irony either..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:39:34-07:00","id":944466,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">In retrospect, since we know the outcome and we\u2019re hoping to change it, modern weapons would be nice, but not necessary. Knowing what the enemy\u2019s going to do is a huge (Yuge!) advantage.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Helms Deep: Instruct the elves to look for unarmored orcs running with a torch; these will be priority targets.<br /> Gondor: Instruct trebuchets to look for a large structure that doesn\u2019t look like the rest of Mordor\u2019s siege engines. It\u2019s a good bet this will be the battering ram. Once located, make that the priority target. </span><br /> Gondor, however, is working under a much tighter time crunch. The battering ram takes its sweet time getting to the gate, but my more serious cousins were quick to take out the trebuchets with their felbeasts. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T18:52:39-07:00","id":944645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/934687-